or ice melting or to manage road conditions; magnesium chloride for use as a road treatment agent for deicing and dedusting; brines for use in oil and gas industry to support well workover and completion activities; and metal recovery salts. The company was founded in 2000 and is based in Denver, Colorado.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kevin S. Crutchfield | CEO & Director | Age 64 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 478 people. Revenue per employee of $624K ranks in the below the sector median among Basic Materials peers. Each employee generates $53K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $11K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Intrepid Potash, Inc is a small-cap basic materials business with a $440M market cap on $298M of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 2% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 18% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $26M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.99\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 46\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 19% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 101% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.01455107292907},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Basic Materials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Environmental remediation liability \u2014 tightening regulations on emissions, tailings, and water use create open-ended balance-sheet risk that grows with each legislative cycle.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 53% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Among the least levered in Basic Materials \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Intrepid Potash (NYSE:IPI) Announces Earnings Results","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/intrepid-potash-nyseipi-announces-earnings-results.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793897811.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.